# fixedbugs, defect 143, panel 185 R1, lane ffi-macro, 2026-10-02.
#
# The macro beside the function-like one: `#define LIMIT 100` is a VALUE, and
# a `constant` binds it, as it has since panel 038. The refused round asks
# whether `LIMIT` is a macro, and it is; the answer is read only where clang
# could not reach a name as anything else, so `LIMIT` stays bound and only
# `SQUARE`, which clang can reach as nothing, is told as a macro. The line
# without an annotation is the half of the case that must stay silent.

extern "fixedbugs-143-macros.h"
    constant LIMIT: i64
    function SQUARE(x: i32) -> i32  #~ ffi_macro_name

function main()
    print(LIMIT)
    print(SQUARE(x: 3))
